  "reason": "The only moderately strong result so far is config_001, RNA-only with PCA_n2000 and singleprofile, with validation accuracy 0.4849 and F1 0.4639, while image-only ResNet50 is much weaker at 0.2079. The key uncertainty is whether the RNA-only result can be improved by using multiprofile aggregation without changing the RNA representation. config_002 keeps the same RNA-only model setting and PCA_n2000 encoder as config_001 but tests multiprofile with avgpool, making it a direct, low-risk comparison that isolates the effect of profile/aggregation. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the most promising current direction while avoiding confounding changes to RNA encoder, image modality, or fusion, and it will clarify whether multiprofile aggregation is worth further exploration before testing transformer aggregation or more complex multimodal models."
}

